        "original_id": "9b0b4428-9f38-5087-94ec-fd6263250b2b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Lane, Lucille Ball, Jim Brochu\n- TV Series: I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, The Lucy Show, Here's Lucy, Life with Lucy\n- Works: Lucy in the Afternoon, MythBusters\n- Roles: supporting actor, authority figure, comedic foe, author\n\nFacts:\n- Lucille Ball was best known as the star of the self-produced sitcoms I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, The Lucy Show, Here's Lucy, and Life with Lucy.\n- Charles Lane was a favored supporting actor of Lucille Ball.\n- Lucille Ball often used Charles Lane as a no-nonsense authority figure and comedic foe for her scatterbrained TV character on I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, and The Lucy Show.\n- Jim Brochu was a friend of Lucille Ball.\n- Jim Brochu wrote the unauthorized biography Lucy in the Afternoon.\n- Jim Brochu appeared on an episode of MythBusters in connection with his role as the author of Lucy in the Afternoon.",
